.TH CLOPS_GPSEXPORT 1 "May 2026" "v2.9.2" "CamClops - GPS Exporter"
.SH NAME
clops_gpsexport \- non-interactive GPS track exporter for dashcam trips
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clops_gpsexport
\fIMID\fR:\fITID\fR
.RB [ \-\-gpx
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-kml
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-geojson
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clops_gpsexport
exports the GPS track for a dashcam trip to one or more file formats without
navigating the interactive GPS menu
.RB ( camclops\ \-G ).
It is suitable for scripting, batch export, and pipeline use.
.PP
If the trip's GPS track has not yet been extracted,
.B clops_gpsexport
runs ExifTool extraction automatically and stores the result in the manifest
before writing any output files.  Subsequent invocations for the same trip
skip extraction and write directly from the cached track.  Extraction runs
at most once per invocation regardless of how many output formats are
requested.
.PP
A trip is addressed by its
.IR MID : TID
(e.g.\&
.BR CQ:73 ),
where
.I MID
is the two-character manifest ID and
.I TID
is the two-character trip ID.  Both are case-insensitive; ambiguous characters
are normalised
.RB ( O\(→0 ,
.BR I\(→1 ,
.BR L\(→1 ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-gpx " PATH"
Write a GPX 1.1 track file.
.TP
.BI \-\-kml " PATH"
Write a KML 2.2 track file with a
.B gx:Track
element containing per-point timestamps, speed, and heading.
.TP
.BI \-\-geojson " PATH"
Write a GeoJSON FeatureCollection (RFC 7946) with one LineString feature.
Coordinates are in
.RI [ longitude ,\  latitude ]
order per the spec.
.PP
At least one format flag is required.  Multiple flags may be combined in a
single invocation; GPS extraction runs only once.
.SS "PATH resolution"
.TP
PATH omitted
Auto-name the output file in the current directory using the trip's start
timestamp as the stem (e.g.\&
.IR 20260209_043838.gpx ).
.TP
PATH ends with /
Auto-name in the specified directory.
.TP
PATH is an existing directory
Auto-name in that directory.
.TP
PATH is a full file path
Use that path exactly.  Extension is appended if missing.
.SS "Other options"
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite existing output files without prompting.  Without this flag,
.B clops_gpsexport
exits with an error if an output file already exists.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show ExifTool stderr during GPS extraction.  Useful for diagnosing extraction
failures or understanding minor tag warnings.  Has no effect if extraction is
skipped (track already in manifest).
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the CamClops version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Progress messages (extraction dots, status lines) are written to
.BR stderr .
Exported file paths are written to
.B stdout
on success, one path per line.  This makes the output pipeable:
.PP
.RS
.nf
clops_gpsexport CQ:73 --gpx /tmp/ | xargs -I{} cp {} /media/usb/
.fi
.RE
.SH "GPS EXTRACTION"
If GPS has not been extracted for the trip,
.B clops_gpsexport
runs ExifTool on every Front camera segment and stores the resulting track
(one point per second) in the trip manifest.  The manifest MD5 is updated
automatically so
.B \-\-validate
does not flag the file as externally modified.
.PP
The ExifTool binary path is read from
.IR ~/.config/camclops/camclops.json .
See
.BR camclops (1)
section
.B GPS EXTRACTION
for details on the format string and camera compatibility.
.SH "OUTPUT FORMATS"
.SS "GPX 1.1"
Produces a standard GPX track with one
.B <trkpt>
per GPS record.  Each point includes latitude, longitude, an ISO 8601
timestamp, and speed in metres per second as a
.B <extensions>
element.  Elevation is omitted for Pruveeo D90 footage (altitude values
are unreliable on that model).
.SS "KML 2.2"
Produces a KML document containing start and end placemarks and a
.B gx:Track
element with per-point timestamps, coordinates, speed, and heading in
.B ExtendedData
arrays.  The track line style is solid red; start pin is green, end pin
is red.  Compatible with Google Earth and other KML viewers.
.SS "GeoJSON (RFC 7946)"
Produces a FeatureCollection with one Feature containing a LineString
geometry.  Properties include
.BR creator ,
.BR trip_id ,
.BR date ,
.BR start_time ,
.BR duration ,
.BR segment_count ,
and
.BR point_count .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Export GPX only, auto-named in current directory:
.B clops_gpsexport CQ:73 --gpx
.TP
Export KML to an explicit path:
.B clops_gpsexport CQ:73 --kml /mnt/maps/trip.kml
.TP
Export all three formats in one pass:
.B clops_gpsexport CQ:73 --gpx /tmp/ --kml /tmp/ --geojson /tmp/
.TP
Force overwrite of existing files:
.B clops_gpsexport CQ:73 --gpx /tmp/trip.gpx --force
.TP
Show ExifTool output during extraction:
.B clops_gpsexport CQ:73 --gpx /tmp/ --verbose
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/camclops.json
Application settings including
.BR exiftoolPath .
GPS extraction arguments are stored in the camera profile embedded in the manifest.
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/manifests.json
Manifest index used for MID:TID resolution.
.TP
.I <footage_path>/clops_manifest_<id>.json
Trip manifest.  Updated in-place after GPS extraction.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All requested output files written successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: MID:TID not resolved, GPS extraction failed, output file exists
without
.BR \-\-force ,
or a write error occurred.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR camclops (1),
.BR clops_gpsinfo (1),
.BR clops_ls (1),
.BR exiftool (1)
